==Trivia==
*The Battle Cats Unite JP Version and the SEA Version are treated as separate versions with the SEA Version currently not receiving any updates.
*Kabuto Cat and Kuwagata Cat are currently the only Switch-Exclusive Cats to be made available for free via login bonus.
*Patch 1.0.6 is the first update to contain new level content (Heavenly Tower) since the release of the game, taking 1,667 days.
*Despite of the September 15, 2023 Update Patch replacing UBERFEST with SUPERFEST, units who were exclusive to the UBERFEST banner still states in their unknown unit description that they are "From Rare Capsule Event UBER FEST."
*Though Piledriver Cat had its trait target ability changed to target all types, this is no longer the case as of Patch 1.0.6 as it does not target Zombies, making its description on the official Unite page inaccurate.
*Curling Cat has had the widest addition to release gap taking 336 days (or 11 months).
*Manga Cat has had the widest gap between Switch-exclusive content being 1,247 days after the addition of Mallet Cat and Undies Cat Jr.
*The game currently totals to about 650 MB with all updates installed, but when broken down:
**The base game is 302 MB.
**Patch 1.0.4, introducing VS Mode and other minuscule additions, is only 52 MB.
**Patch 1.0.5, which introduced multi-language support and other changes, is only 274 MB.
**Patch 1.0.6, which introduced the Heavenly Tower, Advents, and a myriad of other units, is only 22 MB.
**Patch 1.0.1, 1.0.2, 1.0.3, 1.0.7, and 1.0.8 are in kilobytes.
**Though Patch 1.0.9 barely changed the file size, most of it was due to text files being updated from renaming Black enemies to Dark enemies.
*As of Patch 1.0.9, the '''International''' ('''WW''') version has a larger file space than the '''Japanese''' ('''JP''') version, sized at 682 MB versus 650 MB respectively.
*As of October 25, 2026, the International and Japanese versions have been deviated, with the International version having description differences in Patch 1.0.3.

